o=A.aqe(B.aQ.cd(0,'{\n    "questionDetailsPaginated": {\n        "docs": [\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d4f",\n                "s_no": 11,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>As Product Owner in an Agile team, how do you risk-adjust a backlog with features assigned a dollar value for ROI?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Note the risk impact in dollars against the return in dollars and then reprioritize the backlog"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Adjust the backlog to focus on the largest features first"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Capture known risks for each feature and then place cards to control the risks and prioritize in the backlog"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Create a risk register for the project and have it signed off by the risk owners"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "A",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>Assign a dollar value to the risk impact relative to ROI, then reprioritize the backlog to address the features with higher net value first.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.354Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.354Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d4f"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d50",\n                "s_no": 12,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>As an Agile Project Manager, how should the team handle backlog items with the highest risk?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Change the requirements to remove the risk"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Schedule the risk items later in the project so you can deliver maximum value first"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Schedule the risk items earlier in the project to reduce the risk impact over time"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Place high-risk items in a \\"risk iteration\\", where the focus is on reducing risk"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "C",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>Risk is highest early in the project before items have been completed. Completing them first reduces overall project risk.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [\n                    "<div><div><p style=\\"margin:0; padding:0;\\"><b>Risk Score</b> = <b>Probability</b> x <b>Impact</b></p><p style=\\"margin:0; padding:0;\\"><br>The formula to analyze risk severity for a feature is to assign a <i>Probability score</i> and an <i>Impact score</i> to each risk, then multiply them.</p></div></div>"\n                ],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.354Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.354Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d50"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d51",\n                "s_no": 13,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>Which Agile method involves making quality everyone\'s responsibility, leveraging team skills, and minimizing reliance on external inputs?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Servant Leadership"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Sprint Planning"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "The daily stand-up"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "The whole team approach"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "D",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>The whole team approach involves integrating all necessary people into the project team, ideally in a co-located space with cross-functional team members.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.354Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.354Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d51"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d52",\n                "s_no": 14,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>As Agile team lead, what is your next step when an issue is raised during a team retrospective?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Perform fishbone analysis"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Perform Kano analysis"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Perform regression analysis"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Perform multi-vari-chart analysis"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "A",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>Discover the issue\'s root cause. Of these options, Fishbone (or Ishikawa) analysis is the best tool for root cause analysis.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [\n                    "<div><div><ul style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0;\\"><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><b>Kano analysis</b> is used to understand and categorize <b>preferences for product features</b>.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><b>Regression analysis</b> is a statistical technique that <b>model</b><b>s</b><b> relationships</b>, which is more applicable in quantitative analysis and not well-suited for identifying root cause.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><b>Multi-vari chart analysis</b> is used to analyze the sources of variation in a process, making it suitable for process improvement but not the ideal tool for exploring a potential root cause.</div></div></li></ul></div></div>",\n                    "<div style=\\"margin-top:12px;\\"><div><p style=\\"margin:0; padding:0;\\"><b>The Agile Manifesto</b><b>\'s 12 Principles</b><b>:</b></p><ol style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0 0 0 16px;\\"><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">1)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Our highest priority is to satisfy the customer through early and continuous delivery of valuable software.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">2)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Welcome changing requirements, even late in development. Agile processes harness change for the customer\'s competitive advantage.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">3)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Deliver working software frequently, from a couple of weeks to a couple of months, with a preference to the shorter timescale.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">4)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Business people and developers must work together daily throughout the project.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">5)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Build projects around motivated individuals. Give them the environment and support they need and trust them to get the job done.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">6)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">The most efficient and effective method of conveying information to and within a development team is face-to-face conversation.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">7)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Working software is the primary measure of progress.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">8)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Agile processes promote sustainable development. The sponsors, developers, and users should be able to maintain a constant pace indefinitely.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">9)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Continuous attention to technical excellence and good design enhances agility.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">10)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Simplicity--the art of maximizing the amount of work not done--is essential.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">11)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">The best architectures, requirements, and designs emerge from self-organizing teams.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"num-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.0em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"num-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">12)</div><div class=\\"num-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">At regular intervals, the team reflects on how to become more effective, then tunes and adjusts its behavior accordingly.</div></div></li></ol></div></div>"\n                ],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.355Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.355Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d52"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d53",\n                "s_no": 15,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>What technique helps quantify cost risks and their impact?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Value analysis"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Parametric estimating"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Monte Carlo simulation"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Earned Value Management"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "C",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>Monte Carlo simulation helps identify cost variations and is a risk quantification tool that uses probability distributions to compute potential outcomes specifically for project costs.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [\n                    "<div><div><p style=\\"margin:0; padding:0;\\">Monte Carlo Analysis (MCA) is a statistical method used to model uncertainty and predict outcomes by simulating a range of scenarios. It relies on random sampling of variables within probability distributions to evaluate the impact. Key aspects include:</p><ul style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0;\\"><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><b>Random Sampling</b></div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><b>Repetition</b>: The process is repeated thousands or millions of times to generate a distribution of possible outcomes.</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><b>Output Analysis</b></div></div></li></ul><p style=\\"margin:0; padding:0;\\">MCA is widely used in fields such as finance, engineering, project management, and risk assessment to evaluate complex systems and decision-making scenarios as it can capture joint effects of multiple variables to provide realistic variability estimates. However, it can be computationally intensive and requires well-defined inputs.</p></div></div>"\n                ],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.355Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.355Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d53"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d54",\n                "s_no": 16,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>What financial tool calculates the present value of cash outflows minus the present value of inflows?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "IRR"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NPV"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Benefit to cost ratio"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "ROI"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "B",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>Net Present Value evaluates investment profitability by discounting cash flows using a specified rate. A positive NPV indicates a financially viable investment. The formula is as such:</p><div><ul style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0;\\"><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">NPV = Net Present Value<div class=\\"nb-detected-continuation\\"> Rt = Net cash flow at time t</div><div class=\\"nb-detected-continuation\\"> i = Discount rate</div><div class=\\"nb-detected-continuation\\"> t = Time of the cash flow</div></div></div></li></ul></div><p><br><img data-img-index=\\"0\\" data-original-mime=\\"image/jpeg\\" src=\\"https://pmpep.s3.amazonaws.com/file_1781515275082.webp\\" style=\\"width:576px; height:356px;\\"><br>Net Present Value (NPV) assesses investment profitability by discounting cash flows at a specific rate. A positive NPV suggests a viable investment.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.355Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.355Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d54"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d55",\n                "s_no": 17,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>Your Sponsor has committed to building a high-speed rail from an inland city, Ambra, to the coast. Given the <b>odds</b>, <b>cost</b> of the route of $10,000,000, and <b>rewards</b> of the routes in this decision tree, what is the total Expected Monetary Value (EMV) of the route to Bella, given a cost of $10,000,000?</p><br><p><img data-img-index=\\"0\\" data-original-mime=\\"image/jpeg\\" src=\\"https://pmpep.s3.amazonaws.com/file_1781515275174.webp\\" style=\\"width:576px; height:356px;\\"></p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "-2.0 million"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "0.8 million"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "1.6 million"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "10.8 million"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "B",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>EMV = (Probability x Outcome 1) + (Probability x Outcome 2)<br>EMV = (0.8 x 12,000,000) + (0.2 x 6,000,000)<br>EMV = ($9,600,000) + ($1,200,000)<br><b>EMV = $10,800,000</b><b>.</b><br>With the cost of the route being $10,000,000, the net = $800,000 or.8 million; thus, this is a worthwhile investment.<br>Key Point: <b>EMV = \u03a3 </b>(Probability of Outcome \xd7 Monetary Value of Outcome). Sum the EMVs of different outcomes when&nbsp;they represent all the possible results of a single option.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.356Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.356Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d55"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d56",\n                "s_no": 18,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>Which of the following forms typically represent the cost performance baseline?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "P-curve"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Pie curve"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "S-curve"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Symmetric curve"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "C",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>The S-curve displays cumulative costs over time, and is used to track and compare project performance against the planned baseline:<br><img data-img-index=\\"0\\" data-original-mime=\\"image/jpeg\\" src=\\"https://pmpep.s3.amazonaws.com/file_1781515275261.webp\\" style=\\"width:576px; height:356px;\\"></p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.356Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.356Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d56"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d57",\n                "s_no": 19,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>Which of the following <b>three</b> subsidiary plans are integrated into the Project Management Plan?</p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Scope Baseline"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Requirements Management Plan"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Scope Management Plan"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "Cost Management Plan"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "B, C, D",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>Several subsidiary plans are integrated into the overall Project Management Plan, and <i>may</i> include the:</p><div><ul style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0;\\"><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><i>Scope</i> Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><i>Requirements</i> Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Schedule Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\"><i>Cost</i> Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Quality Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Resource Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Communication Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Risk Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Procurement Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Stakeholder Engagement Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Configuration Management Plan</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Change Management Plan, and</div></div></li><li style=\\"list-style:none; margin:0 0 4px 0; padding:0;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-item-grid\\" style=\\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4em 1fr;column-gap:0.35em;align-items:start;\\"><div class=\\"bullet-marker\\" style=\\"display:block;text-align:right;line-height:1.4;\\">\u2022</div><div class=\\"bullet-body\\" style=\\"display:block;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;\\">Compliance Management Plan</div></div></li></ul></div><p>\u2026and more!<br>The Scope Baseline is <b>not</b> a subsidiary plan.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.356Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.356Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d57"\n            },\n            {\n                "_id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d58",\n                "s_no": 20,\n                "text": {\n                    "EN": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"question_text\\"><div data-col=\\"question_text\\"><p>The Gantt chart below displays the schedule status for a construction project. Two activities, Select Site and Negotiate Lease, are completed. 50% of the third activity, Perform Civil Works, <i>should have been</i> completed. However, no work has been done on the third activity. What is the project\'s Schedule Performance Index (SPI), and what does this mean?<br>Hint: Schedule Performance Index (SPI) = Earned Value (EV)/Planned Value (PV).</p><br><p><img data-img-index=\\"0\\" data-original-mime=\\"image/jpeg\\" src=\\"https://pmpep.s3.amazonaws.com/file_1781515275385.webp\\" style=\\"width:576px; height:356px;\\"></p></div></div>"\n                },\n                "question_image": null,\n                "options": [\n                    {\n                        "id": "A",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "The project is behind schedule with an SPI of 0.5"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "B",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "The project is on schedule with an SPI of 1.0"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "C",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "The project is behind schedule with an SPI of 2.0"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "D",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "The project is behind schedule with an SPI of-$10,000"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "E",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "F",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "G",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "H",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    },\n                    {\n                        "id": "I",\n                        "text": {\n                            "EN": "NA"\n                        },\n                        "image_url": null\n                    }\n                ],\n                "correct_answer_id": "A",\n                "marks_per_question": 1,\n                "minus_marks_per_question": 0.5,\n                "explanation_in_english": "<div class=\\"cell-rich\\" data-col=\\"explanation\\"><p>The project has an SPI of 0.5, with the project behind schedule.<br>The logic is below:<br><b>Schedule Performance Index (SPI) = Earned Value (EV)/Planned Value (PV).</b><br>Earned Value (EV) = Planned Value x Percent Complete:<br>EV = ($5,000 x 1) + ($5,000 x 1) <b>EV = $10,000</b><br>for the first two activities. For Planned Value (PV), since the third activity <i>should</i> be 50% complete:<br>PV = ($5,000 x 1) + ($5,000 x 1) + ($20,000 x.5)<br>PV = $5,000 + $5,000 + $10,000<br><b> PV = $20,000</b><br>for the first three activities. Since<br>SPI = EV/PV: <b>SPI = $10,000/$20,000 = 0.5</b><br>Since the SPI of 0.5 is less than 1.0, the project is behind schedule.</p></div>",\n                "explanation_image": null,\n                "active": true,\n                "is_error": false,\n                "train": [],\n                "flip_back": [],\n                "flip_front": [],\n                "error": [],\n                "__v": 0,\n                "createdAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.357Z",\n                "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T09:21:19.357Z",\n                "id": "6a2fc40fc40ebece41165d58"\n            }\n        ],\n        "totalDocs": 115,\n        "limit": 10,\n        "totalPages": 12,\n        "page": 2,\n        "pagingCounter": 11,\n        "hasPrevPage": true,\n        "hasNextPage": true,\n        "prevPage": 1,\n        "nextPage": 3\n    },\n    "myvalue": {\n        "page": "2"\n    },\n    "error": [],\n    "msg": []\n}'))
